#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054611 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67b307f2-1d37-5741-8972-cbddae50c4c8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Product of Two Functions"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e509944-2a4b-5a63-911e-9fc4952ba2fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-13595" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=x+2$ and $g(x)=x-5$, find $(fg)(-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $(fg)(x)$ means  the product of the functions  $f(x)$ and $g(x).$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo evaluate $(fg)(-1),$ we find $f(-1)$ and $g(-1),$ and then multiply the results.\n\nFirst, we find $f(-1)$ and $g(-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =(-1)+2=1 \\\\ g(-1) & =(-1)-5=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply the results:\n\n$$\n(fg)(-1)=f(-1)g(-1)=1\\cdot (-6)=-6\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we find $(fg)(x)$ by multiplying the two functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(fg)(x) & =(x+2)(x-5) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-5x+2x-10 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-3x-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate $(fg)(-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(fg)(-1) & =(-1)^{2}-3(-1)-10 \\\\  & =1+3-10 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e8b25b3-5cc4-51b7-8ff9-fc1773797ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Sum or Difference of Two Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "191ed9fb-e1ea-5bef-892a-5baa90256a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413837} {:answer/id #uuid "2d90ba2d-f17e-5fdb-9818-2e1002340d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413838} {:answer/id #uuid "325859ee-224e-52c1-a505-c5197b9a6558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413839} {:answer/id #uuid "65020d93-ef32-58e5-bf24-738b6719f093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413841} {:answer/id #uuid "e7666301-e17b-5314-afdb-d7835e5ea1bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65020d93-ef32-58e5-bf24-738b6719f093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413841} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4da891c-9eb7-5195-a3f8-0ac1c8c6f04f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23a164f0-a08a-5974-9621-a6231dc1af90" :question/math-academy-id "q-66137" :question/problem "Given $f(x)=2x+1$ and $g(x)=-3x+5,$ find $(f+g)(4).$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $(f+g)(x)$ means the sum of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x).$\n\n**Method 1**\n\nTo evaluate $(f+g)(4),$ we find $f(4)$ and $g(4),$ and then add the results.\n\nFirst, we find $f(4)$ and $g(4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) & =2(4)+1=9 \\\\ g(4) & =-3(4)+5=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we add the results:\n\n$$\n(f+g)(4)=f(4)+g(4)=9+(-7)=2\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we find $(f+g)(x)$ by adding the two functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(x) & =(2x+1)+(-3x+5) \\\\  & =-x+6 \\\\  & =6-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate $(f+g)(4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(4) & =6-4=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
